 "id": "pick-tiers-full",
 "name": "Pickaxe and numeral take the tier",
 "optionNote": "The ⛏ and the effort numeral both take the tier ink, so the change shows with colour icons too (through the numeral). The cost: the numeral loses the enchant pink that says \"enchantment level\", and a netherite Ⅴ is the dimmest text on the line (2.9:1 on its glint). Diamond and stone numerals look like ordinary text, and the purple glint behind them is then the only sign of the effort.",
 "title": "The pickaxe's material follows the model",
 "intro": "Minecraft tools come in tiers: stone, iron, gold, diamond, netherite. Here the pickaxe in hotbar slot 1 takes the tier of the model in use: Fable netherite, Opus diamond, Sonnet iron, Haiku gold (the fastest tool and the quickest to wear out), and any other model stone. What 1.0 draws today (src/hud/mix.ts, TIER): Opus #55FFFF, Fable #9D8F8F, Sonnet #D8D8D8, Haiku #8F8F8F and any other model #AAAAAA, with the effort numeral in the enchant pink #FF55FF. So Opus is already diamond and an unknown model already stone; the visible changes are Haiku (grey to gold), Fable (a darker netherite #857579) and Sonnet (#D8D8D8 to iron #C6C6C6, barely). Important: with colour icons ⛏ is a colour emoji that ignores Hungerbar's colours, so the pickaxe looks the same for every model there, today and in these options. Only Plain icons show its tier; the numeral (Yu Gothic UI) takes the colour in both styles.",
